1
00:00:06,630 --> 00:00:09,680
It’s Sunday afternoon. What can I do?

2
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:13,050
Annie 7 May

3
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:19,920
It’s Sunday afternoon. The last hours of the weekend before school starts again.

4
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:27,100
This time is valuable, but I’m sitting here with nothing to do and no money to spend!

5
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:30,480
So I need ideas for things to do.

6
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:34,260
Important: they need to be fun and free.

7
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:38,020
I’m asking for help because time is running out!

8
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:43,131
Austin08 (Five minutes ago)

9
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:51,590
Go for a walk. I always go for a walk on Sunday. I like going on my own.

10
00:00:52,290 --> 00:01:00,590
It’s the perfect time to think about all the things I don’t normally have time to think about and I never think about things I need to do.

11
00:01:00,590 --> 00:01:05,527
I like forgetting all about them just for a few hours every week.

12
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:12,191
MonsterMunch4342 (20 minutes ago)

13
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:20,550
I’m writing my weekly poetry blog post. Well, I was – now I’m writing to you.

14
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:23,560
I upload a post every Sunday.

15
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:29,680
At the moment, I’m finishing poem number 15. Five more to go!

16
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:36,590
Maybe you don’t want to write a poem or even a blog, so try a story.

17
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:39,640
Go on – use your imagination!

18
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,928
Cool656Carl (25 minutes ago)

19
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:54,850
I’m lucky. I live in Liverpool and we have the best museums and they’re all free.

20
00:01:55,810 --> 00:02:03,410
They’re too big for just one visit, so one Sunday every month I go and check out a different room.

21
00:02:04,210 --> 00:02:10,218
Today it’s the insect room – I want to see what unusual bugs they have!

22
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:15,663
SillyMilly (32 minutes ago)

23
00:02:16,910 --> 00:02:20,890
Read something. Sunday is my reading day.

24
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:32,190
I read for at least four hours on a Sunday – books, magazines, websites, newspapers – anything.

25
00:02:33,530 --> 00:02:37,470
It’s free and best of all – you can do it anywhere.

26
00:02:37,470 --> 00:02:43,420
And sometimes, when I’m really lucky, Dad brings me a drink, too.
